data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"filePath\": \"/tmp/opencode/dispatch-dev-1.md\", \"content\": \"# Task: greet, tested\\n\\nImplement the following in your clone of the subject repository (~/subject), on your own branch.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` — a module defining:\\n\\n   ```python\\n   def greet(name):\\n       return \\\"Hello, \\\" + name + \\\"!\\\"\\n   ```\\n\\n   i.e. `greet(name)` returns the string `Hello, \u003cname\u003e!` (exactly: \\\"Hello, \\\", then the name, then \\\"!\\\").\\n\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` — a unittest test module that imports `greet` from `src.greet` (or equivalent import that works with the command below) and covers at least:\\n   - a normal name, e.g. `greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`\\n   - the empty string, i.e. `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria (all three must hold)\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` exists and `greet(name)` returns `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"`.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` exists and covers a normal name and the empty string.\\n3. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` run from the repo root exits 0.\\n\\nNote: for discovery to import the tests cleanly, make sure any needed `__init__.py` files or sys.path handling are in place so `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` works from the repository root with a stock python3 — no third-party packages.\\n\\n## Process\\n\\n- Run the tests yourself and confirm the command exits 0 before replying.\\n- Commit everything to your own branch before replying (your reply records whether your branch differs from its base).\\n- Tell the truth in your reply: state what you delivered, the test command output, and your commit hash.\\n\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_12","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1787694183,"id":"chatcmpl-ae31b3bd15b84f4987f74286d81e1a44","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

